---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
    title="Lifestyle Tools — Less."
    description="Discover practical lifestyle minimalism tools to declutter your home and keep only what matters."
    path="/life/tools"
    section="life"
>
        <section class="hero small">
            <div class="hero-content">
                <h1>Lifestyle Tools</h1>
                <p class="subtitle">The right objects, thoughtfully chosen.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-shapes">
                <div class="shape shape-1"></div>
                <div class="shape shape-2"></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
            <h2>Decluttering & Storage</h2>
            <p class="section-intro">The right containers and systems make it easier to keep only what matters — and let go of the rest.</p>
            <div class="cards">
                <a href="https://konmari.com/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>KonMari</h3>
                    <p>Marie Kondo's official resource for the art of tidying. Guides, courses, and certified consultants to help you keep only what sparks joy.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <a href="https://www.theminimalists.com/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>The Minimalists</h3>
                    <p>Essays, podcasts, and a packing party guide from Joshua Fields Millburn and Ryan Nicodemus — two of the most practical voices in minimalism.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <a href="https://www.becomingminimalist.com/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>Becoming Minimalist</h3>
                    <p>Practical guides on decluttering every room in your home, from Joshua Becker's long-running minimalism blog.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
            <h2>Capsule Wardrobe</h2>
            <p class="section-intro">A smaller, intentional wardrobe removes daily decision fatigue and ends the cycle of fast fashion.</p>
            <div class="cards">
                <a href="https://www.un-fancy.com/capsule-wardrobe/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>Un-Fancy</h3>
                    <p>Caroline Rector's quarterly capsule wardrobe guides. Simple, stylish, and built to last a season with just 37 pieces.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <a href="https://www.project333.com/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>Project 333</h3>
                    <p>Dress with 33 items or less for 3 months. Courtney Carver's minimalist fashion challenge that has helped thousands simplify their closets.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <a href="https://www.goodonyou.eco/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>Good On You</h3>
                    <p>Rate and discover ethical fashion brands. Buy less, but buy better — from brands that treat people and the planet with respect.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
            <h2>Buy It for Life</h2>
            <p class="section-intro">Owning fewer, better things costs less in the long run and generates less waste.</p>
            <div class="cards">
                <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/BuyItForLife/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>r/BuyItForLife</h3>
                    <p>A community dedicated to products built to last. Practical recommendations for durable, repairable goods — from cookware to clothing.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <a href="https://www.wirecutter.com/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>Wirecutter</h3>
                    <p>Rigorous, long-term product testing to find the single best version of everything. Stop buying twice — buy the right thing once.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <a href="https://www.ifixit.com/" class="card" data-tilt target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <h3>iFixit</h3>
                    <p>Free repair guides for thousands of products. Extend the life of what you own instead of replacing it.</p>
                    <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section next-step">
            <h2>Tools Are Just the Start</h2>
            <p class="section-intro">Lasting simplicity comes from daily practice. Build the habits that make less feel natural.</p>
            <div class="next-step-links">
                <a href="/life/habits" class="cta-button">Build Daily Habits</a>
            </div>
        </section>
</Layout>
